# SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000142  -  CAT II
# The web server must display a default hosted application web page, not a
# directory listing, when a requested web page cannot be found.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000142
group:           V-206411
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001312
control_rev5:    SI-11

contribution:    Splunk Web can deny the enumeration the requirement is aimed at outright
                 rather than mask it per directory: tools.staticdir.generate_indexes
                 determines whether the web server serves a directory listing for static
                 directories at all, and simple_error_page determines the content of the
                 page returned when a requested page cannot be found.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] tools.staticdir.generate_indexes not_equals 1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] tools.staticdir.generate_indexes https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Placing a default page in every web document directory, which the fix text
                 directs literally: the content of the static document directory below
                 $SPLUNK_HOME is carried by the app packaging and the installation's file
                 layout, not by any Splunk setting.
external:        The directories in scope are bounded by web.conf [settings] static_dir,
                 static_endpoint and root_endpoint (web.conf.spec:308, 303, 297), which the
                 assessor reads to scope the check; they define where the document
                 directory is exposed and do not themselves decide the requirement.
external:        Any directory listing served by a front-end web server, object store or
                 CDN mapped into the same URI space is carried by that component and
                 assessed against its own baseline.

citation:        SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000142 check, fix and discussion text (CCI-001312,
                 SI-11 a); no product STIG rule shares CCI-001312. Splunk 10.x
                 specification set (Version 10.0.0): web.conf.spec:333
                 tools.staticdir.generate_indexes = [1 | 0], default 0, documented as
                 controlling whether the webserver serves a directory listing for static
                 directories; scoping keys web.conf.spec:297 root_endpoint,
                 web.conf.spec:303 static_endpoint, web.conf.spec:308 static_dir;
                 web.conf.spec:227 simple_error_page.
finding:         web.conf [settings] tools.staticdir.generate_indexes is set to 1, so
                 Splunk Web generates a directory listing for a static document directory
                 instead of denying the enumeration outright; this is assessed at the
                 application layer alone, and the placement of a default page in each web
                 document directory is recorded as an external dependency carried by the
                 app packaging and the installation's file layout rather than as part of
                 this finding.
